WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.100
One reference episode covering every settings panel, so every later video can just say “see E44” instead of re-explaining.

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.000
Worth bookmarking.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.652
Eight panels total: General, Providers, Media models, Voice, Memory, Devices, Usage, and Data & updates.

4
00:00:12.652 --> 00:00:17.000
We have touched most of these already — this is the map that ties them together.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.636
The search box at the top matches on what a setting does, not what it is called.

6
00:00:20.636 --> 00:00:26.000
Type “interrupt” and it finds barge-in, because that is the behavior, even though the word never appears in its label.

7
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.166
Every panel uses the same draft-and-save model.

8
00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:30.654
Changes show an unsaved marker until you press Ctrl+S.

9
00:00:30.654 --> 00:00:36.000
Navigate away with unsaved changes and it confirms before discarding them — nothing is written until you tell it to.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:45.181
If you only change a handful of settings, make it these: spend caps, the voice engine, speech rewrite, auto-compact, the embedding model, background mode, and how much of the context window memory is allowed to use.

11
00:00:45.181 --> 00:00:48.000
Every one of them has come up already in this series for a reason.

12
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.318
A few things people go looking for and will not find: a per-tool default model, cloud sync, and a memory share above the twenty-five percent ceiling.

13
00:00:54.318 --> 00:01:00.000
Each is a deliberate absence, not a missing feature — simplicity, no account to sync to, and protecting the context window on purpose.

14
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.164
One update worth flagging: new chats now enable the built-in tools by default, rather than starting empty.

15
00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:11.000
That is a starting point, not a standing “enable everything forever” switch — you still trim it down per chat, the same habit from Module 7 about fewer tools choosing better.

16
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.656
Settings covered the app's own configuration.

17
00:01:12.656 --> 00:01:17.000
Next we go deep on one panel specifically — Memory — the three scopes it tracks and the budget that keeps it in check.

